  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Finance, Government of the Republic of Sudan - Sudan (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan, RSSH, Federal Ministry of Health of the Republic of Sudan (MOH)This program has the following goals: Improved health status of the population of Sudan especially the poor, underserved, disadvantaged and vulnerable populations. The objectives of this program are: Improve the meaningful engagement of community based civil society organizations and networks to promote health service utilization and address inequalities related to gender, sexual and human rights.  To develop a sustainable and integrated Health Information System, that provides comprehensive, quality health related information in support of evidence-based policy and planning at different system level.  To develop a well-performing and multitasked facility and community level health workforce to expand and improve the quality of integrated health care services at primary health care level..  To ensure that the health system financing is sustainable, efficient and equitable and provides social protection to the people.  To improve equitable access to quality essential pharmaceuticals and health technologies..  To improve equitable coverage and accessibility of quality integrated primary health care; with special focus to vulnerable and disadvantaged populations.  To strengthen effective leadership, good governance, accountability and adressing policy and legal barriers to access services</narrative>
  </description>
